*G-62 is the normal identical formation of kakugawari koshikake gin. However there's a gote's strategy of intentionally losing turns by playing G-52.
*It turns out that G-52, ittezurashi is actually rather complicated and not necessarily favoring gote. Maybe it can even be said it favors sente. 
*G-62, the normal identical formation of kakugawari leads to many complicated lines, those that are less complicated usually favor sente, so maybe gote wants to try something else. (Actually, we will return to this move anyway)
*One such option is G-72.
*However while G-72 could potentially lead to gote's advantage, it's complicated and sente has a way of avoiding it. So Gote will try to lose one turn by first playing G-62 and THEN G-72. Having said that, sente will probably still have an advantage even in that variation.
